AFTER LIZZY WAS BORN.

237
00:09:34,657 --> 00:09:36,284
OH!

238
00:09:36,284 --> 00:09:38,578
SO YOU RAISED HER
ALL ON YOUR OWN?

239
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,579
YES, I DID.

240
00:09:40,579 --> 00:09:42,499
OH! OH...

241
00:09:44,292 --> 00:09:46,627
All:
HEY.

242
00:09:46,627 --> 00:09:49,047
HOW WAS YOUR FIRST DAY?
PRETTY GREAT.

243
00:09:49,047 --> 00:09:51,174
I DID GET A LITTLE ATTITUDE
FROM THE ROBOT.

244
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:52,800
DAMN THOSE ROBOTS.

245
00:09:52,800 --> 00:09:56,304
THEY'RE SUPPOSED TO BE
OUR FAITHFUL SERVANTS!

246
00:09:56,304 --> 00:09:58,473
ANYWAY, IT WASN'T THE ROBOT,
IT WAS THE GUY WHO CONTROLS HIM.

247
00:09:58,473 --> 00:09:59,974
YEAH, HE DOESN'T LIKE ME.

248
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:02,227
HE HAD C.H.E.E.S.E. KNOCK OVER
THE SANDWICH TABLE

249
00:10:02,227 --> 00:10:03,686
RIGHT WHEN I WAS REACHING
FOR ONE-- OH!

250
00:10:03,686 --> 00:10:06,481
SO WHY DON'T YOU
JUST GET HIM FIRED?

251
00:10:06,481 --> 00:10:08,066
I MAY HAVE TO.

252
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:10,277
I HATE TO DO IT,
BUT I'M THE STAR, YOU KNOW?

253
00:10:10,277 --> 00:10:12,070
THERE'S A LIMIT
TO HOW MANY SANDWICHES

254
00:10:12,070 --> 00:10:13,863
I CAN EAT OFF THE FLOOR.

255
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:15,574
( cell phone rings )

256
00:10:15,574 --> 00:10:16,616
EXCUSE ME.

257
00:10:18,076 --> 00:10:20,579
JOEY TRIBBIANI.

258
00:10:20,579 --> 00:10:22,247
JOE! I'M GLAD I FOUND YOU!

259
00:10:22,247 --> 00:10:23,748
I GOT AN AUDITION FOR YOU!

260
00:10:23,748 --> 00:10:25,166
Wow!

261
00:10:25,166 --> 00:10:27,461
The thing is,
it's kind of on the Q.T.

262
00:10:27,461 --> 00:10:29,588
THE ACTOR WHO HAS THE PART

263
00:10:29,588 --> 00:10:31,881
DOESN'T KNOW HE MIGHT BE FIRED.

264
00:10:31,881 --> 00:10:33,967
It's a lead in a series--

265
00:10:33,967 --> 00:10:35,802
MAC AND C.H.E.E.S.E.

266
00:10:37,512 --> 00:10:39,556
I'M THE LEAD IN
MAC AND C.H.E.E.S.E.!

267
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:41,849
UH-OH!

268
00:10:43,977 --> 00:10:45,520
JOEY?

269
00:10:47,314 --> 00:10:50,024
HI, ROSS.

270
00:10:51,859 --> 00:10:55,696
I WAS JUST GETTING HIM
TO LIKE YOU.

271
00:11:02,912 --> 00:11:04,331
JOEY!

272
00:11:05,373 --> 00:11:06,416
JOEY?!

273
00:11:06,416 --> 00:11:07,584
HEY, ROSS.

274
00:11:07,584 --> 00:11:10,462
ROSS, JOEY IS NOT HERE.

275
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:12,755
OKAY, I'LL JUST
WAIT FOR HIM IN HERE.

276
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:13,798
ROSS, IT'S OKAY.

277
00:11:13,798 --> 00:11:14,924
YOU CAN COME OUT.

278
00:11:14,924 --> 00:11:16,217
YEAH, ROSS, IT'S OKAY.

279
00:11:16,217 --> 00:11:19,513
IT'S ME, MR. STEVENS.

280
00:11:19,513 --> 00:11:20,972
PAUL, I DIDN'T...

281
00:11:20,972 --> 00:11:24,309
OH, MY GOSH,
I DIDN'T EVEN SEE YOU.

282
00:11:24,309 --> 00:11:25,560
SURE YOU DID.

283
00:11:25,560 --> 00:11:27,103
YOU CAME IN,
YOU GOT ALL AWKWARD.

284
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:28,355
YOU RAN TO THE BEDROOM.

285
00:11:28,355 --> 00:11:29,939
YOU WERE SHOUTING
"JOEY! JOEY!"

286
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,943
BYE, RACHEL.
BYE.

287
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:34,944
I'LL CALL YOU LATER.

288
00:11:34,944 --> 00:11:36,196
OKAY. SEE YOU.

289
00:11:36,196 --> 00:11:39,282
BYE, ROSS.

290
00:11:39,282 --> 00:11:40,575
WHAT...

291
00:11:40,575 --> 00:11:43,786
WHAT... HOW...
WHAT THE... HOW... WHAT?

292
00:11:43,786 --> 00:11:46,581
WELL, YOU KNOW, HE LOST HIS KEYS

293
00:11:46,581 --> 00:11:49,000
SO HE WAS LOOKING FOR THEM.

294
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:50,709
IN YOUR MOUTH?

295
00:11:52,837 --> 00:11:54,713
NO...

296
00:11:54,713 --> 00:11:56,966
DOWNSTAIRS,
AND WE GOT TO TALKING,

297
00:11:56,966 --> 00:11:57,967
YOU KNOW, FOR, LIKE, TWO HOURS

298
00:11:57,967 --> 00:11:59,469
AND I REALLY LIKED HIM.

299
00:11:59,469 --> 00:12:01,221
SO I INVITED HIM UP HERE
FOR A CUP OF COFFEE.

300
00:12:01,221 --> 00:12:04,307
YOU WERE AT THE COFFEE HOUSE.

301
00:12:04,307 --> 00:12:06,560
ROSS, WHAT'S THE BIG DEAL?

302
00:12:06,560 --> 00:12:08,311
SO I KISSED THE GUY.

303
00:12:08,311 --> 00:12:11,231
HE'S MY GIRLFRIEND'S FATHER,
OKAY?

304
00:12:11,231 --> 00:12:12,649
IT'S... IT'S WEIRD.

305
00:12:12,649 --> 00:12:14,234
YOU DATED MY SISTER.

306
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:15,902
THAT WAS DIFFERENT.

307
00:12:15,902 --> 00:12:17,070
WHAT? WHY?

308
00:12:17,070 --> 00:12:21,241
THIS IS WEIRD FOR ME.

309
00:12:21,241 --> 00:12:22,367
ROSS, LOOK, LOOK...

310
00:12:22,367 --> 00:12:23,784
THIS IS GOOD
FOR YOU, OKAY?

311
00:12:23,784 --> 00:12:25,119
LET'S FACE IT.

312
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,121
SO FAR,
THE GUY'S NOT LOVING YOU

313
00:12:27,121 --> 00:12:28,998
BUT I CAN TURN THAT AROUND.

314
00:12:28,998 --> 00:12:30,584
I GOT THE INSIDE TRACK.

315
00:12:30,584 --> 00:12:33,002
WE CAN ALL GO OUT TO DINNER.

316
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:35,213
YOU KNOW, AND I
CAN TALK YOU UP.

317
00:12:35,213 --> 00:12:39,509
PLUS, THE GUY IS A VERY,
VERY SUCCESSFUL LAWYER.

318
00:12:39,509 --> 00:12:41,052
HOW IS THAT IMPORTANT?

319
00:12:41,052 --> 00:12:42,803
OH, IT'S IMPORTANT.

320
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,475
SO, APPARENTLY, THERE'S, LIKE,
A MILLION GUYS OUT THERE

321
00:12:47,475 --> 00:12:48,685
THAT CAN PLAY MAC.

322
00:12:48,685 --> 00:12:50,270
AND THERE'S ONLY
THIS ONE ROBOT

323
00:12:50,270 --> 00:12:52,021
AND THIS ONE GUY
WHO CONTROLS IT.

324
00:12:52,021 --> 00:12:53,940
I DIDN'T KNOW
HE COULD GET ME FIRED.

325
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:54,982
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

326
00:12:54,982 --> 00:12:56,401
WELL, YOU KNOW, JOEY

327
00:12:56,401 --> 00:12:58,403
YOU'RE A PRETTY
CHARMING GUY.

328
00:12:58,403 --> 00:13:00,779
THANKS, BUT I KIND OF HAVE
A PROBLEM TO DEAL WITH HERE.

329
00:13:00,779 --> 00:13:03,366
NO, SWEETIE,
YOU'VE GOT TO
WIN OVER THE GUY

330
00:13:03,366 --> 00:13:04,367
WHO CONTROLS C.H.E.E.S.E.

331
00:13:04,367 --> 00:13:05,619
YOU GOT TO GO BACK THERE

332
00:13:05,619 --> 00:13:08,371
AND KISS SOME
SERIOUS ROBOT ASS.

333
00:13:09,456 --> 00:13:11,874
THAT'S NOT A BAD IDEA.

334
00:13:11,874 --> 00:13:13,585
OKAY, BUT IF I GOT TO TURN ON
THE CHARM TOMORROW

335
00:13:13,585 --> 00:13:16,630
I'M NOT WASTING ANY MORE OF IT
OVER HERE WITH YOU GUYS.

336
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:19,215
WELL, ACTUALLY, I GOT A LITTLE
BIT SAVED FOR YOU, PHEEBS.

337
00:13:22,510 --> 00:13:25,221
SO YOU DO YOU THINK, UH,
JOEY'S MORE CHARMING THAN ME?

338
00:13:25,221 --> 00:13:28,391
YEAH. THAT'S WHY I'M SLEEPING
WITH HIM ON THE SIDE.

339
00:13:28,391 --> 00:13:29,934
YEAH, YOU WISH.

340
00:13:33,396 --> 00:13:35,940
"YOU WISH."

341
00:13:35,940 --> 00:13:37,358
PHOEBE, STOP
WRITING ABOUT US.

342
00:13:37,358 --> 00:13:38,985
I'M NOT WRITING ABOUT YOU.

343
00:13:38,985 --> 00:13:40,987
I'M WRITING ABOUT OTHER PEOPLE.

344
00:13:42,029 --> 00:13:43,030
WHO?

345
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,741
MARSHA AND CHESTER.

346
00:13:46,075 --> 00:13:47,076
OKAY, FINE, FINE.

347
00:13:47,076 --> 00:13:48,161
THEN YOU KNOW WHAT?

348
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:50,413
I WILL JUST WRITE
ABOUT PHYLLIS.

349
00:13:50,413 --> 00:13:52,749
"PHYLLIS IS SITTING
IN A CHAIR."

350
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:53,874
OOH.

351
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:55,042
I SEE WHAT YOU'RE DOING.

352
00:13:55,042 --> 00:13:56,336
"PHYLLIS SEES WHAT I'M DOING."

353
00:13:56,336 --> 00:13:58,004
OOH-HOO.

354
00:13:58,004 --> 00:14:03,259
OOH, I HAVE TASTED MY OWN
MEDICINE AND IT IS BITTER.

355
00:14:08,556 --> 00:14:10,391
MORNING. HEY...

356
00:14:10,391 --> 00:14:13,227
HOW'S MY FAVORITE GENIUS
AND HIS LITTLE ROBOT BUDDY?

357
00:14:13,227 --> 00:14:14,228
DON'T TOUCH HIM.

358
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:16,397
OKAY. ALL RIGHT.

359
00:14:16,397 --> 00:14:18,566
UH, ALL RIGHT,
WAYNE... LOOK

360
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:19,776
LEVEL WITH ME, OKAY?

361
00:14:19,776 --> 00:14:21,235
I KEEP HEARING
ALL THESE RUMORS

362
00:14:21,235 --> 00:14:22,445
THAT I MIGHT GET FIRED.

363
00:14:22,445 --> 00:14:23,863
THEY EVEN HAVE
ACTORS COMING IN

364
00:14:23,863 --> 00:14:25,615
TO READ FOR MY PART.

365
00:14:25,615 --> 00:14:26,907
COME ON, MAN.

366
00:14:26,907 --> 00:14:28,284
YOU GOT TO GIVE ME
A SECOND CHANCE.

367
00:14:28,284 --> 00:14:30,370
I MEAN, I LOVE
THIS LITTLE GUY...

368
00:14:30,370 --> 00:14:32,372
OKAY.

369
00:14:32,372 --> 00:14:34,374
THAT'S WHY YOU
DIDN'T WANT ME TO
TOUCH HIM, RIGHT?

370
00:14:34,374 --> 00:14:37,418
HERE YOU GO.

371
00:14:37,418 --> 00:14:38,419
STUPID...

372
00:14:38,419 --> 00:14:39,587
I CAN'T BELIEVE IT.

373
00:14:39,587 --> 00:14:40,547
GOD...

374
00:14:41,756 --> 00:14:44,217
HEY, HOW YOU DOING?

375
00:14:49,930 --> 00:14:51,932
SO, IT SEEMED
THAT MY PROM DATE

376
00:14:51,932 --> 00:14:55,436
HAD STOOD ME UP,
SO ROSS SELFLESSLY

377
00:14:55,436 --> 00:14:58,272
OFFERED TO TAKE ME.

378
00:14:58,272 --> 00:15:00,692
WHAT A NICE STORY.

379
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:01,860
SO ROSS WAS IN COLLEGE

380
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:03,611
AND DECIDED TO JUMP
AT THE CHANCE

381
00:15:03,611 --> 00:15:05,946
TO TAKE A YOUNG GIRL
TO HER HIGH SCHOOL PROM.

382
00:15:07,990 --> 00:15:09,492
WOW...

383
00:15:09,492 --> 00:15:12,328
I DEFINITELY DID NOT SEE
THAT ONE BACKFIRING.

384
00:15:12,328 --> 00:15:14,288
I'M GOING TO GO
TO THE BATHROOM.

385
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:16,416
YEAH, TAKE YOUR TIME.

386
00:15:18,752 --> 00:15:20,086
YOU KNOW, JUST SO YOU KNOW

387
00:15:20,086 --> 00:15:21,128
I WAS A FRESHMAN
AND SHE WAS A SENIOR.

388
00:15:21,128 --> 00:15:23,005
SO IT WASN'T AS BAD AS...

389
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,966
ROSS, LOOK, I KNOW I
HAVE BEEN GIVING YOU
A LOT OF JABS

390
00:15:25,966 --> 00:15:30,263
AND IT'S PARTLY
BECAUSE I'M VERY
PROTECTIVE OF LIZZY

391
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:33,933
AND PARTLY BECAUSE, WELL,

392
00:15:33,933 --> 00:15:37,437
THEY JUST KEEP COMING TO ME.

393
00:15:37,437 --> 00:15:38,897
BUT I HAVE TO
ADMIT THAT AFTER

394
00:15:38,897 --> 00:15:40,939
ALL THE WONDERFUL THINGS
LIZZY HAS TOLD ME

395
00:15:40,939 --> 00:15:44,485
AND THE MANY, MANY,
MANY STORIES

396
00:15:44,485 --> 00:15:45,570
THAT RACHEL
HAS TOLD ME

397
00:15:45,570 --> 00:15:48,406
THAT, WELL...

398
00:15:50,408 --> 00:15:53,870
YOU'RE NOT... ALL BAD.

399
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:58,666
"NOT ALL BAD."

400
00:15:58,666 --> 00:16:00,460
AND YOU KNOW, I'M SORRY
I WAS SO HARSH BEFORE

401
00:16:00,460 --> 00:16:01,586
BUT YOU HAVE TO UNDERSTAND

402
00:16:01,586 --> 00:16:03,713
I STILL LOOK AT LIZZY

403
00:16:03,713 --> 00:16:06,173
LIKE SHE'S A
12-YEAR-OLD GIRL.

404
00:16:06,173 --> 00:16:07,258
YEAH, YOU KNOW WHAT?

405
00:16:07,258 --> 00:16:08,426
I KNOW WHAT YOU MEAN.

406
00:16:08,426 --> 00:16:11,846
I DO THAT, TOO.

407
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:12,847
I BEG YOUR PARDON.

408
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:14,265
NO, NO, I'M NOT...

409
00:16:14,265 --> 00:16:16,893
I DON'T MEAN I SEE HER
AS A 12-YEAR-OLD GIRL.

410
00:16:16,893 --> 00:16:18,937
I MEAN,
I HAVE A SON WHO'S SIX

411
00:16:18,937 --> 00:16:21,147
AND I STILL THINK OF HIM
AS A BABY.

412
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,231
YOU HAVE A SON?

413
00:16:22,231 --> 00:16:23,858
WELL, MY EX-WIFE AND I

414
00:16:23,858 --> 00:16:25,318
SHARE CUSTODY OF BEN

415
00:16:25,318 --> 00:16:27,069
AND, UH, JUST
SO YOU KNOW

416
00:16:27,069 --> 00:16:29,530
CAROL AND I ARE
ON EXCELLENT TERMS

417
00:16:29,530 --> 00:16:31,991
AS I'M SURE YOU ARE
WITH YOUR WIFE.

418
00:16:31,991 --> 00:16:32,951
OH, I'M SORRY.

419
00:16:34,619 --> 00:16:36,454
IT'S UNBELIEVABLE.

420
00:16:36,454 --> 00:16:37,956
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

421
00:16:37,956 --> 00:16:40,040
I JUST DIDN'T REALIZE
YOU WERE MARRIED.

422
00:16:40,040 --> 00:16:42,293
OH, WE WERE, BUT
THAT WAS JUST A...

423
00:16:46,172 --> 00:16:49,759
I MEAN, THAT WAS JUST
A BIG DRUNKEN MISTAKE.

424
00:16:52,637 --> 00:16:54,054
YOU'RE BACK.

425
00:16:56,265 --> 00:16:58,434
YOU TWO WERE MARRIED?

426
00:16:58,434 --> 00:17:00,728
OH, WHOOPS, I'M SORRY.
YOU WERE TALKING ABOUT EMILY.

427
00:17:04,148 --> 00:17:05,692
CHANDLER, WE SAID
WE WOULD MEET

428
00:17:05,692 --> 00:17:07,902
AT THE COFFEE HOUSE AT 6:00.

429
00:17:07,902 --> 00:17:09,195
WE SAID 7:00.

430
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,530
WE SAID 6:00.

431
00:17:10,530 --> 00:17:12,824
THE ONLY WAY
THAT I SAID 6:00

432
00:17:12,824 --> 00:17:15,242
WOULD BE IF I SAID
THE SENTENCE:

433
00:17:15,242 --> 00:17:17,954
"LET'S MEET AT 7:00,
NOT AT 6:00."

434
00:17:17,954 --> 00:17:19,455
YEAH, AND IF I HAD SAID 7:00

435
00:17:19,455 --> 00:17:21,165
MAYBE I WOULD HAVE SAID
SOMETHING LIKE THIS:

436
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:24,126
"WOW, MY BOYFRIEND
IS SUCH A WISE ASS, 7:00."

437
00:17:25,503 --> 00:17:26,504
HI.

438
00:17:26,504 --> 00:17:28,297
OH, MY GOOD GOD.

439
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:30,132
I KNOW WHAT
TIME YOU SAID.

440
00:17:30,132 --> 00:17:31,175
WHAT?

441
00:17:31,175 --> 00:17:32,969
WELL, ACTUALLY, I KNOW WHAT TIME

442
00:17:32,969 --> 00:17:34,721
CHESTER AND MARSHA SAID.

443
00:17:35,972 --> 00:17:37,431
WHAT TIME?

444
00:17:37,431 --> 00:17:38,975
HMM, QUITE AN INTERESTING
TURN OF EVENTS.

445
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:41,686
SUDDENLY, IT'S MY BOOK
TO THE RESCUE, HUH?

446
00:17:41,686 --> 00:17:42,729
LET'S SEE.

447
00:17:42,729 --> 00:17:45,439
OOH, VERY INTERESTING.

448
00:17:45,439 --> 00:17:47,692
YEAH, WELL, THIS CERTAINLY
CLEARS THINGS UP.

449
00:17:49,235 --> 00:17:50,236
WHAT DOES IT SAY?

450
00:17:50,236 --> 00:17:51,738
I WILL TELL YOU

451
00:17:51,738 --> 00:17:53,447
AS SOON AS YOU THANK ME
FOR WRITING MY BOOK.

452
00:17:55,324 --> 00:17:56,910
THANK YOU
FOR WRITING YOUR BOOK.

453
00:17:56,910 --> 00:17:58,828
IT'S A GREAT BOOK

454
00:17:58,828 --> 00:18:02,707
AND YOU ARE THE QUEEN
OF EVERYTHING.

455
00:18:03,791 --> 00:18:05,835
THANKS, SO ARE YOU.

456
00:18:10,757 --> 00:18:13,760
TOLD YOU I SHOULD NOT WEAR
THIS COLOR.

457
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:19,766
"MONICA... MARSHA AND CHESTER

458
00:18:19,766 --> 00:18:22,977
"ARE PLANNING ON
SEEING A MOVIE
SUNDAY NIGHT.

459
00:18:22,977 --> 00:18:25,104
"MARSHA THINKS THEY'RE SUPPOSED
TO MEET AT 6:00.

460
00:18:25,104 --> 00:18:28,274
CHESTER THINKS IT'S AT 7:00."

461
00:18:28,274 --> 00:18:30,443
SO YOU KNEW
WE WERE GOING TO MISS THE MOVIE?

462
00:18:30,443 --> 00:18:31,444
THAT'S RIGHT.

463
00:18:31,444 --> 00:18:32,737
INSTEAD OF TELLING US

464
00:18:32,737 --> 00:18:34,447
YOU WROTE IT IN
YOUR STUPID BOOK?

465
00:18:34,447 --> 00:18:38,785
"MARSHA AND CHESTER
ARE MAD AT PHYLLIS."

466
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,960
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I'M GOING TO LOSE THIS JOB.

467
00:18:46,960 --> 00:18:48,210
OH, I'M SO SORRY, MAN.

468
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,796
IS THERE ANYTHING I CAN DO?

469
00:18:49,796 --> 00:18:51,714
YEAH. HELP ME
GET THIS MINI FRIDGE

470
00:18:51,714 --> 00:18:53,424
PAST THE SECURITY GUARD.

471
00:18:53,424 --> 00:18:55,927
( knocking )

472
00:18:58,972 --> 00:19:01,724
HEY, JOEY, I WANT
TO TALK TO YOU.

473
00:19:01,724 --> 00:19:03,559
YEAH, WELL, I DON'T
WANT TO TALK TO YOU, WAYNE.

474
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:04,602
I HATE YOU.

475
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,395
YOU RUINED MY LIFE.

476
00:19:06,395 --> 00:19:07,396
OH. CHANDLER, WAYNE.
WAYNE, CHANDLER.

477
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:09,107
HI, HOW ARE YOU?

478
00:19:09,107 --> 00:19:13,402
JOEY, JOEY, I'LL GET YOU YOUR
JOB BACK IF YOU HELP ME OUT.

479
00:19:13,402 --> 00:19:15,404
WHY SHOULD I HELP YOU OUT?

480
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,281
THE REASON
HE JUST SAID.

481
00:19:17,281 --> 00:19:19,700
WHAT DO YOU NEED?

482
00:19:19,700 --> 00:19:22,703
I SAW YOU ON STAGE

483
00:19:22,703 --> 00:19:24,497
TALKING TO THAT
BEAUTIFUL WOMAN.

484
00:19:24,497 --> 00:19:26,082
YOU KNOW, SARAH.

485
00:19:26,082 --> 00:19:27,500
I WISH I COULD
TALK TO HER.

486
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:29,794
WHAT? ARE YOU IN LOVE WITH HER
OR SOMETHING?

487
00:19:29,794 --> 00:19:33,673
YEAH... HER...
ALL OF THEM... ANYONE.

488
00:19:33,673 --> 00:19:37,343
YEAH, I'VE BEEN THERE,
MY FRIEND.

489
00:19:37,343 --> 00:19:39,428
LISTEN, I GUARANTEE
YOU KEEP YOUR JOB

490
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,264
IF YOU CAN TEACH ME HOW
TO TALK TO WOMEN LIKE YOU DO.

491
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,224
OH, WELL, WAYNE...

492
00:19:44,224 --> 00:19:45,977
IT'S NOT REALLY SOMETHING
YOU CAN TEACH, YOU KNOW?

493
00:19:45,977 --> 00:19:47,687
IT'S PRETTY MUCH SOMETHING
YOU'RE BORN WITH...

494
00:19:47,687 --> 00:19:48,688
YOU CAN TEACH IT.

495
00:19:48,688 --> 00:19:50,523
I CAN SHOW YOU HOW TO DO IT.

496
00:19:52,108 --> 00:19:53,776
I MEAN, IF YOU
THINK ABOUT IT

497
00:19:53,776 --> 00:19:55,778
I MEAN, ROSS DID
LEARN SOMETHING

498
00:19:55,778 --> 00:19:57,155
FROM EACH MARRIAGE.

499
00:19:57,155 --> 00:20:00,533
HOW TO MAKE THE NEXT ONE
EVEN SHORTER?

500
00:20:00,533 --> 00:20:01,575
NOW, WAIT A MINUTE.
THAT'S NOT FAIR.

501
00:20:01,575 --> 00:20:03,243
I MEAN, HE WAS
MARRIED TO ME

502
00:20:03,243 --> 00:20:05,371
A HELL OF A LOT LONGER THAN
HE WAS MARRIED TO EMILY.

503
00:20:05,371 --> 00:20:06,622
HE JUST DIDN'T TELL ME.

504
00:20:11,251 --> 00:20:13,087
MAYBE I HAVE
TO PEE AGAIN.

505
00:20:18,176 --> 00:20:20,594
WELL, THIS IS FUN.

506
00:20:20,594 --> 00:20:24,891
SO, ROSS, DID YOU KILL
ANY OF THESE WIVES?

507
00:20:24,891 --> 00:20:25,933
YOU KNOW WHAT?

508
00:20:25,933 --> 00:20:27,518
I HAVE HAD ENOUGH OF THIS.

509
00:20:27,518 --> 00:20:31,147
YOU KNOW, I CARE A GREAT
DEAL ABOUT YOUR DAUGHTER

510
00:20:31,147 --> 00:20:33,315
AND I HAVE TREATED HER
WITH NOTHING BUT RESPECT.

511
00:20:33,315 --> 00:20:36,152
SO, IF YOU GOT A PROBLEM
WITH ME, FRANKLY, I...

512
00:20:36,152 --> 00:20:37,486
ARE YOU YELLING AT ME?

513
00:20:37,486 --> 00:20:39,613
GOD, NO.

514
00:20:39,613 --> 00:20:41,824
YOU KNOW WHAT, DADDY?

515
00:20:41,824 --> 00:20:44,160
IF YOU DON'T LIKE ROSS,
THAT'S FINE.

516
00:20:44,160 --> 00:20:45,828
IT DOESN'T MATTER TO ME.

517
00:20:45,828 --> 00:20:47,997
I'M GOING TO GO OUT
WITH HIM ANYWAY.

518
00:20:47,997 --> 00:20:49,373
REALLY?

519
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:52,085
WELL, IF IT DOESN'T
MATTER TO HER

520
00:20:52,085 --> 00:20:54,170
IT DOESN'T MATTER TO ME.

521
00:20:54,170 --> 00:20:55,629
STILL NOT YELLING.

522
00:20:57,673 --> 00:20:59,508
WELL...

523
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,969
WHAT CAN I SAY?

524
00:21:04,346 --> 00:21:06,264
THIS DOESN'T MAKE ME
LIKE YOU ANY BETTER.

525
00:21:06,264 --> 00:21:08,101
THAT'S OKAY,
I'M NOT SO CRAZY ABOUT MYSELF

526
00:21:08,101 --> 00:21:10,144
RIGHT NOW, EITHER.

527
00:21:10,144 --> 00:21:11,187
THEN WE AGREE?

528
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,605
YEAH, YEAH, I GUESS SO.

529
00:21:12,605 --> 00:21:13,689
NEITHER OF US LIKE ROSS.

530
00:21:13,689 --> 00:21:14,690
I LIKE ROSS.

531
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:17,401
OH... KIDS.

532
00:21:19,737 --> 00:21:21,739
WAIT, WAIT, WAIT.
I JUST THOUGHT
OF ANOTHER STORY

533
00:21:21,739 --> 00:21:23,032
ABOUT HOW NICE
ROSS IS.

534
00:21:23,032 --> 00:21:24,408
UH, IT'S OKAY, RACH.

535
00:21:24,408 --> 00:21:25,826
WE'RE NOT LIKING
ROSS RIGHT NOW.

536
00:21:25,826 --> 00:21:27,285
OH, I GOT A LOT
OF THOSE, TOO.

537
00:21:32,708 --> 00:21:33,834
WELL, IT TURNS OUT

538
00:21:33,834 --> 00:21:35,335
YOU WERE RIGHT, C.H.E.E.S.E.

539
00:21:35,335 --> 00:21:38,089
THE SHIPMENT NEVER MADE IT
THROUGH OMAHA?

540
00:21:38,089 --> 00:21:39,090
YOU GOT IT.

541
00:21:39,090 --> 00:21:40,633
AND THE RABBI'S BEARD--

542
00:21:40,633 --> 00:21:43,094
100% HORSEHAIR.

543
00:21:43,094 --> 00:21:44,720
NICE CATCH, C.H.E.E.S.E.

544
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:51,269
IT'S YOUR LINE, C.H.E.E.S.E.

545
00:21:54,354 --> 00:21:55,564
WAYNE!

546
00:21:55,564 --> 00:21:56,774
WAYNE!

